DAY 56 - PART A: THEORY (REVISION)
Capstone: Everything Together
Time: 30 minutes
==================================================================

Review the whole course in one picture:

  Developer --push--> GitHub --Actions--> image registry
                         |                     |
                     config repo          (pulled by nodes)
                         |
                      Argo CD (in cluster) --sync-->
  +----------------------------- cluster ------------------------------+
  |  Ingress controller (TLS by cert-manager)                          |
  |     |                                                              |
  |  frontend (Deployment, HPA, probes, PDB)                           |
  |     |  DNS: api                                                    |
  |  api (Deployment, HPA, probes, ConfigMap, Secret, SA)              |
  |     |  DNS: db-0.db                                                |
  |  db (StatefulSet + PVC, or managed DB in the cloud)                |
  |  NetworkPolicies: ingress -> frontend -> api -> db only            |
  |  Prometheus/Grafana/Alertmanager watching everything               |
  +--------------------------------------------------------------------+


CAPSTONE REQUIREMENTS
---------------------
 1. 3 tiers: frontend, API, database
 2. Images built by CI and pushed to a registry
 3. A Helm chart OR Kustomize overlays (dev + prod)
 4. Ingress with TLS from cert-manager
 5. Database with persistent storage; config in ConfigMap; password
    in a Secret (not in Git in plain text)
 6. Requests/limits, probes, PDB, topology spread
 7. HPA on the API, tested with a load generator
 8. NetworkPolicies (on a Calico/Cilium cluster) or documented
 9. ServiceMonitor + at least one alert + a Grafana dashboard
10. Deployed by Argo CD; a change in Git reaches the cluster
11. Runs on kind; optionally on EKS for a few hours, then deleted
12. A README describing architecture, how to deploy, how to roll back
